   "sql": "SELECT c.id, c.name, c.city, count(*) AS orders\nFROM customers AS c\nJOIN orders AS o ON o.customer_id = c.id\nWHERE c.name IN ('Sam Lee', 'Ada Lovelace')\nGROUP BY c.id\nORDER BY c.id",
   "note": "grouped by the primary key, each customer is a bucket of their own. city can be selected too: postgres knows id decides it.",
